# The Kiwi Network web catalog: the same shape as kiwi-catalog (one git URL
# per line, optional key=value options after it), for the web side of the
# network. Every entry's repository carries a kiwi.manifest; its CATEGORY
# says what the entry is:
#
#   Framework   the engine a hub is built on (kiwi-framework)
#   Hub         a distribution: one hub, built on the framework, deployed somewhere
#   App         app code a hub can mount; it lives in its own repository, or in
#               a hub's repository under the path= option
#
# Options:
#   path=<dir>       the app's folder inside the repository (apps in a hub's repo)
#   ref=<tag>        pin to an exact version; otherwise the latest version tag, else HEAD
#   branch=<name>    track a branch instead of release tags
#
# This catalog is read by the web tooling (a hub importing another hub's app
# is one line here plus one mount in its distribution.js). The entries are not
# desktop apps: do not add this catalog to the kiwi updater.

# frameworks
https://github.com/derlocke-ng/kiwi-framework.git

# hubs
https://github.com/derlocke-ng/armory.git

# apps shipped by Armory
https://github.com/derlocke-ng/armory.git path=apps/loadout
https://github.com/derlocke-ng/armory.git path=apps/devboard
https://github.com/derlocke-ng/armory.git path=apps/payload
https://github.com/derlocke-ng/armory.git path=apps/pongjs
https://github.com/derlocke-ng/armory.git path=apps/enigmajs
